Fix KLOG so it dumps the CURRENT boot's tracev3 (SpringBoard/backboardd log).

Measured problems:
 1. 0130's per-dump KLOGD line counter is a static that is never reset (cap
    200), so dumps 6..8 printed 0 lines even when files were read.
 2. File selection was arbitrary: the dumps kept reading the same old
    tracev3 files from previous boots while a newer file in the directory
    was ignored.
 3. No per-file byte budget and no clear per-dump header.

0139 (bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c, the 0129/0130/0131 KLOG code):
 - sweet_log_dump() resets sweet_log_lines, sweet_logd_lines and the file
   list at the START of every dump (cap is per dump);
 - the readdir pass now COLLECTS all *.tracev3 entries with their
   modification/change time (vnode_lookup + vnode_getattr va_modify_time /
   va_change_time), sorts them newest-first and processes only the newest
   `sweetklogfiles` files (default 2, hard cap 8);
 - new `sweetklogbytes` per-file read budget (default 262144) applied to both
   the raw and LZ4 read loops in addition to the existing 512 KiB hard cap;
   the LZ4 chunk walker also stops when the per-dump line cap is reached;
 - headers:
     KLOG --- dump N at <uptime> s: files=<n> newest-first (found=<m>), lines=0/<cap>
     KLOG pick i/n <name> mtime=<t>
     ... KLOG file/KLOG|/KLOGZ/KLOGD| lines ...
     KLOG end <n> lines (lz4=<k>)
 - new `sweetkloglines` per-dump line cap (default 200; hard cap 1000);
 - all existing boot args keep working: sweetlogdump / sweetloglz4 /
   sweetlogtimes / sweetlogmax / sweetlogdir (sweetlogmax still sets the cap
   and sweetkloglines overrides it).  Default OFF: no sweetlogdump=1, no work.

Boot args for the next image (unchanged plus the new knobs):
  sweetlogdump=1 sweetloglz4=1 sweetlogtimes=240,420,600
  sweetlogmax=300 sweetkloglines=200 sweetklogfiles=2 sweetklogbytes=262144
